# ── Supabase (PostgreSQL 17, ap-southeast-1) — the project's only database ──
# SQLite→Supabase migration: Prisma datasource now targets Supabase Postgres.
# Connection uses the Supavisor SESSION pooler (IPv4) because the direct
# db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432 endpoint is IPv6-only and unreachable from this
# sandbox (verified: DNS AAAA-only, TCP fail).
#
# IMPORTANT: the datasource reads SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL (NOT DATABASE_URL)
# because this sandbox's harness injects a stale
# DATABASE_URL=file:/home/z/my-project/db/custom.db into every shell session,
# and exported env vars override .env values. A distinct var name is immune.
# NOTE: values are intentionally unquoted — the Prisma CLI does not strip quotes.
SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.tujvscnonmupldrqkqen:Aiman0122769500%21@aws-0-ap-southeast-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require&connection_limit=10&connect_timeout=10

# Direct (non-pooled) connection reference — IPv6-only endpoint, for docs/ops.
# DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres:Aiman0122769500%21@db.tujvscnonmupldrqkqen.supabase.co:5432/postgres

